{"name":"Caribbean Coast","hex":"#93c5dd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"coast","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The edge of the land where it meets an ocean, sea, gulf, bay, or large lake. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The side or edge of something."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To glide along without adding energy; to allow a vehicle to continue moving forward after disengaging the engine or ceasing to apply motive power.","To sail along a coast."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coast"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tung Chung","blocks":[{"text":"Tung Chung is an area on the northwestern coast of Lantau Island, Hong Kong. One of the most recent new towns, it was formerly a rural fishing village beside Tung Chung Bay, and along the delta and lower courses of Tung Chung River and Ma Wan Chung in the north-western coast of Lantau Island. The area was once an important defence stronghold against pirates and foreign military during the Ming and the Qing dynasties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Tung_Chung_2008.JPG/330px-Tung_Chung_2008.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tung_Chung"},{"title":"Caribbean","blocks":[{"text":"The Caribbean is a geo-political region in the middle of the Americas centered around the Caribbean Sea in the North Atlantic Ocean, mostly overlapping with the West Indies. Bordered by North America to the north and also the west through Central America, and South America to the south, it comprises numerous islands, cays, islets, reefs, and banks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png/330px-Central_America_and_the_Caribbean_Shaded_Relief_Map.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Caribbean"},{"title":"Coast","blocks":[{"text":"A coast is the land next to the sea or the line that forms the boundary between the land and the ocean or a lake. Coasts are influenced by the topography of the surrounding landscape and by aquatic erosion, such as that caused by waves. The geological composition of rock and soil dictates the type of shore that is created. Earth has about 620,000.0 km (385,250.1 mi) of coastline."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg/330px-Spring_Lake%2C_New_Jersey_Beach_at_Sunrise.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coast"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg/500px-%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg/1280px-%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg/500px-%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A%E6%9D%B1%E6%B2%96%E9%80%B8%E6%9D%B1%E6%9D%91%E5%85%A8%E6%99%AF.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lantau_Island_1840.jpg/500px-Lantau_Island_1840.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Lantau_Island_1840.jpg/1280px-Lantau_Island_1840.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser